The problem asks to compute $\binom{15}{7}$, and we are given $\binom{14}{8} = 3003$ and $\binom{14}{7} = 3432$. We can use the recursive relationship of binomial coefficients:  
$$
\binom{n}{k} = \binom{n-1}{k-1} + \binom{n-1}{k}
$$  
Applying this to $\binom{15}{7}$, we have:  
$$
\binom{15}{7} = \binom{14}{6} + \binom{14}{7}
$$  
